{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation","id":1397447,"title":"Success of the Usurpation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-18T21:43:53-07:00","id":1397447,"title":"Success of the Usurpation","content":"How the Usurpation could succeed? Of course, the Dragonblooded have the advantage of surprise. However Terrestrial are the weakest of the Exalted, and there are only 100 Sidereals at any given time. Their loyalty is also divided, not all Dragonblooded and Sidereals turn their back to the Mandate. Whereas the Solars and Lunars are at their height; they command unimaginable resource and technology, and probably most of them are High Essence(6+), which make them nigh-invincible. I think even if 100 Solars survive after the initial assassination, it is more than enough number to turn the tide and massacre rebels in turn, let alone their Lunar mates and loyalist Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 06-19-2020, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T21:52:23-07:00","id":1397449,"title":"","content":"The Dragonblooded and Sidereals are also at the height of their power, sitting on reservoirs of unimaginable wonders and war machines. Also, the Solars probably didn't see it coming, and the Solars who managed to sense the growing tension probably suspected their fellow Solar Exalted, rather than their lieutenants and advisors. They'd probably sequester themselves in their fortresses and dominions, where they are alone and are easier to attack.<br /> <br /> The basic story as I see it is: a great amount of Solars, young and old, are gathered together in Meru for the Calibration Feast. Somebody obliterates the entire palace with apocalyptic magic/martial arts and the Solars that don't die instantly are scattered throughout the ruins. Then Sidereals, blazing with the might of their martial arts, ride down from the heavens on Elemental Dragons and Dragon-Blooded warriors, burning like a hurricane of the five elements, storm into the rubble to execute whoever they find.<br /> <br /> As far as opening gambits of what is ultimately a war of Usurpation, it seems pretty cut and dry to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T22:08:32-07:00","id":1397451,"title":"","content":"Solars are powerful, but they're not that powerful, and they're not all focused on being invincible gods. Many of them were legendary crafters or amazing sailors, or loremasters. They would die very quickly when facing a Sidereal assassin and a dozen dragonblooded warriors. There also weren't necessarily that many super elders either, even in 2e the signature Dawn was only Essence 4 at the time of the usurpation because he kept going off into unwinnable battles and getting reincarnated.<br /> <br /> Even for the elder warriors though, as a change for third edition, Essence 6+ doesn't really represent much more of a power increase, other than more motes. It just lets their custom charms be a bit weirder and more personalized, although still extremely potent. <br /> <br /> Also, eventually, they run out of Essence and Willpower and become little more than exceptional mortals, and if they run out before the rebels run out of bodies to throw at the, they die. As Kymmenthe also mentioned, the Sidereals and Dragonblooded were also at the height of their power, with several elder exalted and access to nearly limitless resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T22:23:43-07:00","id":1397454,"title":"","content":"Weakest yes, but not as bad as last edition whereby their perfects didn't work against celestial exalts. Also essence 6+ isn't a common thing in 3rd even in the first age, and if I recall the count of survivors of the Usurpation was 50 or lower in the Solar camp in 2e. (So if your logic is based off 2e when 6+ was a matter of course for everyone including DBs they weren't getting the 1/3 of their numbers your estimating.)<br /> <br /> Now as for tricks potentially used. Well first the Sids and DBs had the advantage of research. Knowing your target is infinitely useful, even just knowing which targets not to apply certain tactics to would be a huge asset; not counting things of more traditional use like weaknesses and battle tactics. The war assets of the targets are also probably screwed because you wouldn't want your targets getting them.So any of those assets the DBs and Sids couldn't use for themselves would likely have had means taken to prevent others from getting them like saying destroying the entrance to armory, so your opponent has to either quickly dig through them or abandon it till a later time that their assailants are aiming to prevent from happening.<br /> <br /> Then of course whenever possible evidence to suggest the attack is being carried about by a rival power or powers. Making it look like a chunk of the deliberative has turned on the individuals grants the usurpers the additional benefit of making it less likely for Solars and Lunars to seek or gain alliances with the others as the potential ally could just be looking for an opportunity to knife them in the back.(Also possible situations where Lunars decided to end their solar would help too.) This is also a perk on the whole not-all-DBs-were-usurpers argument as they were more than likely attacked as enemies when seen even if they protested otherwise, consequently causing more DBs to become adversaries in self-defense.<br /> <br /> This is not counting whatever assets various exigents would have provided as they're complicated and so varied who knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T00:30:44-07:00","id":1397469,"title":"","content":"I'd also like to add something (that may be a bit headcanony) : The Usurpation happens because the Bronze faction Sidereal expected the Solar to destroy the world, and if most DB decided to follow them, it was because the Celestials were proving the Bronze Faction right. The good time of the High First Age were gone, and many Celestial Kingdoms were waging war against one another, feeding the Great Curse between themselves in a neverending cycle. The Solars didn't fight only the Usurpater, they also fought between themselves because they had started to resent each other to the point a whole part of the world decided to rise against them.<br /> <br /> I think it's important to reaffirm the part The Great Curse (or whatever the form you give it) takes in the setting, because the it's the motor of lot of the &quot;Why did it go so bad at the time ?&quot; in the Exalted setting and gameplay.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T03:23:16-07:00","id":1397487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation#post1397447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">probably most of them are High Essence(6+), which make them nigh-invincible.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Third Edition not only goes with an idea that only a minority of Exalted ever breached Essence 5, but the kinds of powers acquired from that aren't really any greater, just more personally iconic. Nothing in the game is nigh-invincible.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T05:10:33-07:00","id":1397493,"title":"","content":"10,000 Dragons conquer the world.<br /> <br /> 30, 40, 50k Dragonblood? They outnumbered the Solars more than a hundredfold. Yes, Solars are more powerful than Dragonblood, but they're certainly not 100 times as powerful.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T07:04:42-07:00","id":1397502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397493#post1397493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">10,000 Dragons conquer the world.<br /> <br /> 30, 40, 50k Dragonblood? They outnumbered the Solars more than a hundredfold. Yes, Solars are more powerful than Dragonblood, but they're certainly not 100 times as powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Of course, you can't fit that many in a room with a Solar all at once.<br /> <br /> The total population of the Dragon Blooded is and always has been an operational concern, not a tactical one. Even at the Calibration Feast, I would not have expected the Solars to have been <i>that</i> outnumbered, and the initial attack is plausibly going to concentrate first on the most martially capable Solars. The ones whom you'd expect to struggle and ultimately fail against even about six Dragon Blooded, they can go second or third, so long as you've established a perimeter that prevents their escape.<br /> <br /> Not all Solars at the feast are killed, and not all Solars even attended the feast, but once they get out into the world they find that the operational scope of the Terrestrial Exalted has allowed them to occupy most of the key positions, cutting off resources and safe havens for the Solars while providing much more for the Dragon Blooded to bring to bear on any given point. You don't need to substantially outnumber the Solars, you just need to make sure that there's no point that they can readily reach at which they won't be encircled by enough to destroy or harass them.<br /> <br /> That also affords the Dragon Blooded the advantage of ground that they can safely retreat to, while also having reserves to immediately move into their place, while the Solar is still wounded and struggling through the mire. Dragon Blooded numbers don't mean you use Zerg Rush tactics, it means that you have people ready in the rearguard to collect and patch up those who need to fall back from the bad fight. Maybe that particular fight was completely one-sided, but if the Solar falls under attack and bloodies the enemy enough for them to retreat, there's often an incentive to let them go rather than chase them down to finish off; your priority in that case is to find a place of safety from which to take stock of your situation and plan your next move. If you get a moment of relieved pressure, you take it to advance towards that objective, not pursue your attackers into their safe haven where you're liable to find more fresh attackers.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Great Curse is in play. The provocations of the attack on the Calibration Feast and any further outrages are liable to have many Solars reacting in distinctly irrational ways that are against their best interests. Considering the underlying mythology of the Curse, an opportunity like the Usurpation is going to be one in which we might expect any Solar in Limit Break to specifically choose the course of action that is least helpful to them at that time. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">there are only 100 Sidereals at any given time</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sidereals possess significant powers for information sorting and mobility and acting with precision. Breakfast in Luthe, dinner in Zarlath, that sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T07:20:55-07:00","id":1397504,"title":"","content":"I agree with the people who say the Usurpation definitely would\u2019ve succeeded irl. It was a cleverly planned and meticulously executed surgical strike, planned by the Bronze Faction Sidereals and carried out by the Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T07:56:27-07:00","id":1397507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397493#post1397493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">10,000 Dragons conquer the world.<br /> <br /> 30, 40, 50k Dragonblood? They outnumbered the Solars more than a hundredfold. Yes, Solars are more powerful than Dragonblood, but they're certainly not 100 times as powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is one of the most underrated points about the Usurpation. There were <i>significantly</i> more Dragon-blooded back then than there are now, and there weren't more Solars (well, technically there were if you remove the Abyssals and Infernals from today's count, but total Solaresque essences remained the same). Not double, not triple, <b>way more</b> Dragon-blooded. It's a valid game-changer in a conflict between the two parties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T15:21:29-07:00","id":1397585,"title":"","content":"I'm not crazy about emphasizing large numbers as:<br /> <br /> 1) it kind of plays down Dragonblooded as individual heroes a bit, and <br /> 2) more crucially, it breaks plausibility of this as a secret-until-the-last-possible-moment coup by the Solars trusted lieutenants. which is to me, what the Usurpation is supposed to be, thematically. 50k Dragonblooded were in on the plan, and then the super-social, super-spy Exalted don't figure it out? if you're talking a plot by perhaps the 2k highest and hand-picked by the Sidereals Dragonblooded, who launch a surgical strike, this at least makes sense to me as something the Sids could plausibly keep under wraps, with a *lot* of effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T15:28:05-07:00","id":1397586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397585#post1397585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not crazy about emphasizing large numbers</div> </div> </div> </div>It also makes the Lunars kind of look like chumps and makes it seem like either Abyssal, Infenal, or Solar dominance of the setting is just kind of inevitable. <br /> <br /> &quot;The Solars are back, things are really going to change.&quot; Is good<br /> &quot;The Solars are back, playtime for the children is over.&quot; Is bad","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T19:09:12-07:00","id":1397605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397585#post1397585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) more crucially, it breaks plausibility of this as a secret-until-the-last-possible-moment coup by the Solars trusted lieutenants. which is to me, what the Usurpation is supposed to be, thematically. 50k Dragonblooded were in on the plan, and then the super-social, super-spy Exalted don't figure it out?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's this thing that happens when big groups organize into hierarchical power structures, where the guys at the bottom don't generally get to know all the fine details about what's going on at the top. If the guys at the top are planning something kinda furtive, they might not make those details clear immediately, especially if there's any reason to believe that the folks on the bottom of the pyramid might object to it if they're not introduced to it by degrees.<br /> <br /> \u200bNot every Dragon-Blooded needed to be informed ahead of the Usurpation that all the Dragon-Blooded were going to be usurping all the Solars. In fact, I'd wager that most of them weren't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-19-2020, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T20:37:32-07:00","id":1397618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397507#post1397507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this is one of the most underrated points about the Usurpation. There were <i>significantly</i> more Dragon-blooded back then than there are now, and there weren't more Solars (well, technically there were if you remove the Abyssals and Infernals from today's count, but total Solaresque essences remained the same). Not double, not triple, <b>way more</b> Dragon-blooded. It's a valid game-changer in a conflict between the two parties.</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually depends. In 2e yeah, there wre a lot (1M DBs). But that is based on some assumptions of DB population growth and ease of replacement to that edition. I think in 3e, while thee were probably more DBs, I tend to get a feel that it wasn't <i>much</i> more than today, whcih is a few centuries of cultivation since the Usupraiton. I kind of tend to imagien DB numbers are fairly stable in teh grand scheme of things. The world's DBs today united would have been enough to give the Solars and Lunars problems. A bit more say, 30k, seems about what could getyou a Shogunate as described in <b>Fangs at the Gate</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T22:39:24-07:00","id":1397626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397618#post1397618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I tend to get a feel that it wasn't <i>much</i> more than today, whcih is a few centuries of cultivation since the Usupraiton. I kind of tend to imagien DB numbers are fairly stable in teh grand scheme of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Balorian Crusade and Great Contagion happened along the way. Numbers were purported to take a significant hit then.<br /> <br /> But, yeah, between progenitive essence and essence fever rules, Ex3 Dragon-blooded population levels are stable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 06-20-2020, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T01:15:23-07:00","id":1397636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397626#post1397626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Balorian Crusade and Great Contagion happened along the way. Numbers were purported to take a significant hit then.<br /> <br /> But, yeah, between progenitive essence and essence fever rules, Ex3 Dragon-blooded population levels are stable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant those actuall, but yeah. DB populations grow slow, but I'm not sure so slow that they're not like, more o rless where they were before the Contagion. Tending towards being rich aristocrats who have the abiltiy to have kids when they need and keep them alive and healthy for a while adds up over a few cneturies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T01:29:06-07:00","id":1397638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397585#post1397585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not crazy about emphasizing large numbers as:<br /> <br /> 1) it kind of plays down Dragonblooded as individual heroes a bit, and<br /> 2) more crucially, it breaks plausibility of this as a secret-until-the-last-possible-moment coup by the Solars trusted lieutenants. which is to me, what the Usurpation is supposed to be, thematically. 50k Dragonblooded were in on the plan, and then the super-social, super-spy Exalted don't figure it out? if you're talking a plot by perhaps the 2k highest and hand-picked by the Sidereals Dragonblooded, who launch a surgical strike, this at least makes sense to me as something the Sids could plausibly keep under wraps, with a *lot* of effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll back you up, I find that trying to explain the setting through a unique explanation downplay the individual importance of each type of hosts. I prefer to think the Usurpation was a complicated moment, that everyone can adapt depending on its expectation of lore and campaign (for example for me it was very decentralized because I don't really adhere to the whole &quot;Solar ONU&quot; thingy, so it was more of different revolutions happening in the Celestial kingdoms to bring down their masters at different time in history) and that's okay that different people want to put forward different things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T01:51:44-07:00","id":1397641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397605#post1397605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's this thing that happens when big groups organize into hierarchical power structures, where the guys at the bottom don't generally get to know all the fine details about what's going on at the top. If the guys at the top are planning something kinda furtive, they might not make those details clear immediately, especially if there's any reason to believe that the folks on the bottom of the pyramid might object to it if they're not introduced to it by degrees.<br /> <br /> \u200bNot every Dragon-Blooded needed to be informed ahead of the Usurpation that all the Dragon-Blooded were going to be usurping all the Solars. In fact, I'd wager that most of them weren't.</div> </div> </div> </div>When that coup against Erdogan happened a couple of years ago, a lot of the soldiers involved in the coup had no idea they were rebels; they thought they were taking down rebels. They were just following the orders of their commanders.<br /> <br /> Also, on Ghosthead's point about security, I can well imagine that a smaller number of DBs attack the Solars, and then a war breaks out across the world. Solars are going crazy, Dragonblood who've been irritated with the Solars for a while go &quot;well, the Solars killed my cousin, and they're raving about murdering all Dragonblood, I'm joining the revolution.&quot; So a few thousand Dragonblood fighting the Solars turns into 30000 Dragonblood fighting the Solars.<br /> <br /> But anyhow. I'm not trying to say &quot;the Usurpation was clearly all about zerg rushing&quot;. That's dull. It just seems a very obvious first answer when people say the Usurpation was impossible. Because anyone who thinks that clearly has never played out an Essence 5 Zenith/Twilight/Night/Eclipse vs five Essence 3 Dragonblood. The one on her own rarely wins.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think it's also worth mentioning the Sidereals. Like, yes, the Dragonblood might have done most of the fighting, but there are 100 Sidereals, let's say 70 get involved, they're almost as powerful as Solars, they're prepared and planned, they're working in teams to assassinate Solars, that's a fairly significant punch into the Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-20-2020, 04:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T02:50:33-07:00","id":1397644,"title":"","content":"Good points Chausse, Alucard, et al. <br /> <br /> Thinking aout this more, I think there's room for a good middle-ground actually, where I'd probably go for it being about 50-70% alpha-strike ambush by an relatively elite group of chosen Dragonblooded, backed up by the Sidereals (both directly in battle and by their destiny-rigging, squirreling away of artefacts, etc.), probably preferentially targeting certain Solars who are more vulnerable to surprise and ambush... then when the advantages of ambush are lost, that's when the Usurpation that really becomes a movement that brings in a much wider pool of Dragonblooded numbers (the 50k or more) used broadly and shallowly (and probably at higher cost of life), to push home the advantage, leveraging family loyalty and dissatisfaction with Solar abuses and sheer social pressure, and that deals with the remaining 50-30%. <br /> <br /> But that's just how I'd perhaps be inclined to see it right now, and perhaps there's some value in a bit of &quot;creative ambiguity&quot; and having &quot;mileage vary&quot; for individual setups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T03:48:48-07:00","id":1397649,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> very good point. I like your bedtime analogy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T03:57:59-07:00","id":1397651,"title":"","content":"Narratively, I have to assume that the Usurpation runs partially on the dramatic conceit of many of the Solars being arrogant enough to presume themselves totally secure, as has been the downfall of many a tyrant in myth, fiction and more than a couple in real life. The resources are there to make the conclusion (although less extreme than some might describe them as), but they're not being applied. That includes the occasion in which a Solar becomes aware of some plotting and then laughs it off as an absurdity.<br /> <br /> The other part is an assumption that the large numbers aren't the part that is important for the planning, but the consolidation when things go down. When word comes down the wire that the honour guard of the Calibration Feast have launched an attack and key positions are being seized all over, it comes down to you to decide which side you're going to pledge yourself to. It is entirely plausible to see this play out in favour of setting consistency as &quot;group loyalty, growing disillusion with the Solars, personal benefit and a healthy dose of fear (both for my fellows if they win and I didn't support and for the Solars who might not give me the chance to pledge loyalty) are enough to make me independently take steps in favour of the Usurpation&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T04:18:41-07:00","id":1397654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397493#post1397493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">10,000 Dragons conquer the world.<br /> <br /> 30, 40, 50k Dragonblood? They outnumbered the Solars more than a hundredfold. Yes, Solars are more powerful than Dragonblood, but they're certainly not 100 times as powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is Solar Sorcery. Solar Wonders and Artifacts. And thousand years of accumulated lore and battle experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397487#post1397487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Third Edition not only goes with an idea that only a minority of Exalted ever breached Essence 5, but the kinds of powers acquired from that aren't really any greater, just more personally iconic. Nothing in the game is nigh-invincible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Dragonblooded can typically live only 250-300 years. Whereas the Celestial Exalted are expected to live more than millennia. It is more than enough time to cultivate their power and break Essence 5. For instance. Lunar Elders in 3rd Edition are Essence 6+.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 06-20-2020, 07:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T04:43:08-07:00","id":1397665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397654#post1397654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is Solar Sorcery. Solar Wonders and Artifacts. And thousand years of accumulated lore and battle experience.<br /> <br /> <br /> Really? Dragonblooded can typically live only 250-300 years. Whereas the Celestial Exalted are expected to live more than millennia. It is more than enough time to cultivate their power and break Essence 5. For instance. Lunar Elders in 3rd Edition are Essence 6+.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing in Solar Sorcery is insurmountable.<br /> <br /> Many-Faced Strangers will give us ancient Lunars with lower Essence.<br /> <br /> Do the Lunar Elder Charms look particularly powerful to you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T04:53:13-07:00","id":1397669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397665#post1397665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing in Solar Sorcery is insurmountable.<br /> <br /> Many-Faced Strangers will give us ancient Lunars with lower Essence.<br /> <br /> Do the Lunar Elder Charms look particularly powerful to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars can nuke Dragonblooded forces with sorcery and wonders. They are, for all intents and purposes, alike modern atomic weapons.<br /> <br /> Who said that?<br /> <br /> No, they aren't seem particularly powerful. But the First Age Solars are breed apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T05:27:26-07:00","id":1397687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397669#post1397669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the First Age Solars are breed apart.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=p2c5qG8uuDc\" target=\"_blank\">*cocks shotgun*</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T05:38:43-07:00","id":1397691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397669#post1397669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars can nuke Dragonblooded forces with sorcery and wonders. They are, for all intents and purposes, alike modern atomic weapons.<br /> <br /> Who said that?<br /> <br /> No, they aren't seem particularly powerful. But the First Age Solars are breed apart.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In 3rd Edition, we intentionally know very little about the First Age Solars.<br /> <br /> One of the things we know about the First Age Solars is .... the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> So however powerful they are, they must have been vulnerable to something the DBs and Sidereals were capable of.<br /> <br /> With regards to modern atomic weapons:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">In the modern world, atomic weapons are used mainly as a deterrent. Anyone who goes up against a foe with atomic weapons would take massive civilian and military casualties. People have also discussed using them to attack soldiers, but there are limitations - if the enemy army is spread out, you're never going to get all of them. If the enemies only need a small assassination team to survive, they can defeat a nuclear power, as long as they are willing to take massive losses.<br /> <br /> Were they?</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3E Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But some escaped this initial ambush, and in the decades that followed the survivors waged terrible wars against the host of the usurpers. During that time, much of the magic of the First Age was lost\u2014expended or destroyed in cataclysmic acts of revenge. In time, the last of the Solars were hunted down and killed, and with them died the First Age.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3E Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Nothing lasts forever.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The fall of the Solars left their Realm a smoking ruin. The curse that had eaten away at them had also eaten away at their works. Without the Solars to steady the sorcerous mechanisms that ran their world, the Realm began to disintegrate. This was no slow winding down, but the agonal throes of a beast mortally wounded. Cities collapsed. Manses rained brimstone on farmlands. Mountains buried themselves, dragging down nations with them. Whole islands were blasted from the seas as the sorceries that </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">birthed them unwound themselves.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Clearly they were willing to, and did, take massive losses from nuclear-like destructive sorcery.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T05:39:07-07:00","id":1397692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397669#post1397669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars can nuke Dragonblooded forces with sorcery and wonders. They are, for all intents and purposes, alike modern atomic weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they aren't. They've got Rain of Doom (strategically useful) and Death Ray (concentrated).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Who said that? </div> </div> </div>The writers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, they aren't seem particularly powerful. But the First Age Solars are breed apart. </div> </div> </div>No, that book introduces the baseline of what elder powers are like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T06:24:19-07:00","id":1397702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397692#post1397692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No they aren't. They've got Rain of Doom (strategically useful) and Death Ray (concentrated).</div> </div> </div> </div>Green Sun. Shrike. Titan Fortresses. Thousand Dragons. To name a few. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397692#post1397692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that book introduces the baseline of what elder powers are like.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that is just about remnant Lunar Elders of the Fallen Age. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T06:24:19-07:00","id":1397703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397692#post1397692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No they aren't. They've got Rain of Doom (strategically useful) and Death Ray (concentrated).</div> </div> </div> </div>Green Sun. Shrike. Titan Fortresses. Thousand Dragons. To name a few. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397692#post1397692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that book introduces the baseline of what elder powers are like.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that is just about remnant Lunar Elders of the Fallen Age. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T06:30:01-07:00","id":1397706,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Rain of Doom (to use the example of a mass attack spell) is obviously good, but it seems not without counters - you disperse your army to not be all under the same area, if you recognize it early, or you use a sorcerer to counter it, which sometimes works? If you even have that many Dragonblooded together in one place in the first place? It's a city-killer, not that much of an army killer<br /> <br /> Solar sorcerers have good tools to prevent huge masses of low-level Dragonblooded being sent against them, but it's not like... &quot;Nice lot of thousands of Dragonblooded you got all standing in a small infantry square there, waitin' around... Shame if something were to... SUDDENLY HAPPEN TO EM!&quot; was that much of a thing, right?<br /> <br /> The strategy to deal with Solars was probably not on the whole to mass really huge amounts of Dragonblooded in one place, and when they knew that a given Solar was really good at mass attack magic, they especially *really* didn't do it. The Sidereals and the elder Dragonblooded were not strategic idiots. I'm sure on some occasions they did have to do it because it was unavoidable, and when they did they really suffered for it - but this probably did not lose them the war, even if meant some hard battles and major losses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T06:39:22-07:00","id":1397709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397703#post1397703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Green Sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even assuming this isn't an exaggeration of Ligier's capabilities, the ritual to summon him takes six hours and needs to be begun at sunset. If you miss that window before Calibration ends, that resource is thoroughly cut off.<br /> <br /> The machines weren't there in the feast hall, and can be the sort of thing the Usurpers moved to hold or cut off first.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, that is just about remnant Lunar Elders of the Fallen Age. </div> </div> </div>How closely have you followed developer statements of the intended portrayal of the setting and function of its writing these last few years?<br /> <br /> That doesn't really matter though. There's a thread for fielding questions to the developers right there, ask them if the gulf between Essence 5 and for Solars is intended to be any more profound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T06:42:37-07:00","id":1397711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397709#post1397709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even assuming this isn't an exaggeration of Ligier's capabilities, the ritual to summon him takes six hours and needs to be begun at sunset. If you miss that window before Calibration ends, that resource is thoroughly cut off.<br /> <br /> The machines weren't there in the feast hall, and can be the sort of thing the Usurpers moved to hold or cut off first.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd even assume that the Usurpers prepared their coup and summoned Ligier in advance to attack the Solars, and also stole a part of their Artifact to attack them on the Usurpation, at that point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T06:46:27-07:00","id":1397713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397711#post1397711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd even assume that the Usurpers prepared their coup and summoned Ligier in advance to attack the Solars, and also stole a part of their Artifact to attack them on the Usurpation, at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon Blooded and Sidereals can't summon Third Circle Demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T07:01:00-07:00","id":1397719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397713#post1397713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dragon Blooded and Sidereals can't summon Third Circle Demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need to summon them yourself, you just need to abuse a Good-willing Solar in a Limit Break to lend them to you temporarily because <i>you need it for something very important</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T07:38:47-07:00","id":1397729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397702#post1397702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Green Sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Solars had begun a tradition of dining together during Calibration to mutually assure each other that as few Third Circle Demons were being summoned into Creation as possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397702#post1397702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shrike.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not finished yet. Technically still unfinished.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397702#post1397702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Titan Fortresses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Turns out that bringing some sort of floating battle fortress to the dinner you're attending is bad manners.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397702#post1397702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thousand Dragons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Turns out that bringing a geomancy-draining war-engine to a region rife with manses and demesnes <i>just so you can attend a dinner</i> is bad manners.<br /> <br /> \u200bBesides, they had their share of Dragon-Blooded bodyguards and lieutenants providing security; they didn't <i>know</i> they were going to be betrayed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-20-2020, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T08:01:39-07:00","id":1397732,"title":"","content":"Oh Please. What I mean is, after the Pearl Harbor is taken. <i>Afterward </i>the true battle for the Creation is commenced.<br /> <br /> And I have serious doubts about Usurpers capability to <i>assassinate </i>the Night Caste. I think they can counter Sidereals pretty well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 06-20-2020, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T08:05:50-07:00","id":1397734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397732#post1397732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh Please. What I mean is, after the Pearl Harbor is taken. <i>Afterward </i>the true battle for the Creation is commenced.</div> </div> </div> </div>World War II would have gone really differently if virtually all the United States' leadership was clustered together in Pearl Harbor for a dinner when the Japanese planes came in.<br /> <br /> Also, please stop moving the goalposts. It's already canon that a number of Night Castes survived the Usurpation and committed a number of acts of sabotage in the years following the Usurpation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-20-2020, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T08:17:26-07:00","id":1397738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397719#post1397719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't need to summon them yourself, you just need to abuse a Good-willing Solar in a Limit Break to lend them to you temporarily because <i>you need it for something very important</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a very strange proposal in terms of the exact timing it would require and the kind of Limit Break that would impair one's judgement sufficient to agree to such a task with such a vague appeal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T08:22:32-07:00","id":1397739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397732#post1397732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh Please. What I mean is, after the Pearl Harbor is taken. <i>Afterward </i>the true battle for the Creation is commenced.<br /> <br /> And I have serious doubts about Usurpers capability to <i>assassinate </i>the Night Caste. I think they can counter Sidereals pretty well.</div> </div> </div> </div>The narrative of the Usurpation typically assumes that the pivotal initial strike of the Usurpation was severe and efficient precisely to prevent the kind of long drawn out conflict that has lesser chances of success and is more likely to bring horrific destruction when it does.<br /> <br /> But sure, Night Castes are supposed to be disproportionately represented among Solars who lasted long enough to not be sealed away. But not every Night Caste at that time was going to be at the height of their power. It is plausible enough that a large amount of force unexpectedly levelled on them at the outset would clear out the least powerful ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T08:26:25-07:00","id":1397740,"title":"","content":"Hmm... It's one thing to say &quot;That they lost is inconsistent with the mechanics&quot;. to which the response would be that the mechanics are representative and not exhaustive, unless anything is too badly out of whack. But it's a tenable thing to discuss. <br /> <br /> It's kind of another to say effectively &quot;That they lost is inconsistent with the facts of the setting&quot;, as the fact that they lost is <i>kind</i> of one of the most key basic establishing facts of the setting. <br /> <br /> Which of these is more your argument Numinous?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T08:51:53-07:00","id":1397746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397651#post1397651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Narratively, I have to assume that the Usurpation runs partially on the dramatic conceit of many of the Solars being arrogant enough to presume themselves totally secure, as has been the downfall of many a tyrant in myth, fiction and more than a couple in real life. The resources are there to make the conclusion (although less extreme than some might describe them as), but they're not being applied. That includes the occasion in which a Solar becomes aware of some plotting and then laughs it off as an absurdity.<br /> <br /> The other part is an assumption that the large numbers aren't the part that is important for the planning, but the consolidation when things go down. When word comes down the wire that the honour guard of the Calibration Feast have launched an attack and key positions are being seized all over, it comes down to you to decide which side you're going to pledge yourself to. It is entirely plausible to see this play out in favour of setting consistency as &quot;group loyalty, growing disillusion with the Solars, personal benefit and a healthy dose of fear (both for my fellows if they win and I didn't support and for the Solars who might not give me the chance to pledge loyalty) are enough to make me independently take steps in favour of the Usurpation&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, and going a little further, I would think we can divide the Usurpation into three stages:<br /> <br /> (1) Planning and surgical strike. Here numbers need to be low, because the utmost secrecy is required. Here the Sidereal's fate-manipulation powers are probably doing the most work, to counteract the Solar's supernatural investigation / intentions-reading abilities. Because this attack has the advantage of complete surprise, and enough planning to stockpile whatever weapons are suitable for destruction on this scale, numbers are not actually needed. One could imagine that the number of Exalts who are fully in on the conspiracy is less than the number of Solars + Lunars, although one could also imagine that Sidereal magic could conceal a far larger cabal.<br /> <br /> (2) The immediate aftermath. Whichever Solars survived the initial assault are on the back foot, but whatever plans the Sidereals and DBs made are quickly going to turn chaotic as well. The Solars are going to be places the usurpers didn't expect them to be, and demonstrate powers the usurpers didn't expect them to have. They are still Solars. Here is where outnumbering the enemy, to deal with these unpredictabilities, will be very helpful for the Bronze Faction side. At this point, it's crucial for them to convince DBs who weren't involved in the initial scheming to take their side over the Solars. I'm imagining a typical scenario involves a Solar who was known not to be at the Calibration Feast for whatever reason having a Sidereal-led assassination team sent against her. She survives the initial assault and kills sum of the assassins, but their backup plan is to rally whichever Dragonblooded are nearby - most likely the Solar's own (hopefully mistreated) subordinates - for a second strike. However the full 100 to 1 numerical advantage is not being used here - more likely 5 to 1, like a modern Wyld Hunt, or 1 Sidereal + 1 DB in on the plotting + 7 of the Solar's personal guard vs. 1 Solar + 3 of the Solar's personal guard. <br /> <br /> (3) The days, weeks, years, and decades after. At this point, the surviving Solars will have had time to consolidate bases of power loyal to them - it will be hard to get them alone. They have armies, and time to figure out where enemy armies are amassing against them. Thus they can start making use of powerful magic like Rain of Doom, God-King's Shrike, powerful artifacts the Sidereals did not steal or destroy, and so on. At this point I would imagine almost every combat-capable Dragonblooded in Creation will end up choosing a side (although Creation at this time was even bigger than it is now so maybe not) and a supermajority, though not quite all, will favor the Usurpers.<br /> <br /> Here the DB's greater numbers are clearly necessary for victory - one can't defeat the Solars in a fair fight on even footing - but their drastic numerical advantage, which is now many hundreds to one (though less vs. lunars) is probably not. They could have made do with far less. Each Solar is still only one person, and I think for this period the Jade Prison is still accepting new guests, so they don't reincarnate. To defeat a Solar, the Dragonblooded only have to get them outnumbered, depending on the Solar, somewhere between two-to-one and ten-to-one. The Solars can try to stop this by hiding in fortresses and surrounding themselves with armies, but the Usurpers have access to many artifacts and sourcerous workings themselves, and can use them to devastating effect. There is also the possibility of lesser betrayals by previously loyal troops, perhaps set off by nasty instances of the Great Curse. Because this war goes on for decades, and most of the Solars are already dead, we only need a kill rate of something like 2 per year here. A lot can go wrong!<br /> <br /> The Sidereals, meanwhile, are reincarnating as normal, and new DBs are constantly growing up - for the first 15-20 years, at exactly the normal rate, and then probably somewhat less for the remainder of the war.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T10:33:14-07:00","id":1397762,"title":"","content":"I wrote a long post and accidentally deleted it, so I'll just hit the high points. Apologies if I don't go into detail or phrase things carefully.<br /> <br /> 1) Essence 6+ First Age Solar Charms are basically the same sort of thing as the Essence 6+ Lunar Charms in <i>Fangs at the Gate</i>.<br /> <br /> 2) In Third Edition, the First Age didn't mollycoddle its Exalts. Solars died while diving head-first into the same perils as the Exalted of the Age of Sorrows: wars and duels, monsters and natural disasters, exploring ancient cities and alien realms, etc. Veterans of the early days of the First Age would have been rare; most would get themselves killed after centuries, decades, or only years after Exaltation.<br /> <br /> 3) Third Edition's history speaks of a Second Deliberative, not a Solar Deliberative. Solars were powerful, prestigious, and overrepresented in the Deliberative, but not every other Exalt owed them fealty.<br /> <br /> 4) The Usurpation happened in the game's history in every edition. Unless you want to run a game set during or immediately after the Usurpation, or you want to run an alternate-history game, a deep dive into exactly what happened at the Calibration Feast is probably not the best use of your time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T11:01:09-07:00","id":1397768,"title":"","content":"Now I'm imagining a character who wants to compose <i>the</i> definitive historical account of the Usurpation, which I imagine is otherwise a complex, messy period that nobody has yet put in the work to investigate and make comprehensible.<br /> <br /> In gameplay terms, that largely amounts to investigating ruins and locating and interviewing knowledgeable figures, with actions to represent composing and recounting discrete portions in appropriate circumstances to get a desired reaction rather than actually track the full scope of the project.<br /> <br /> Something between Ovid's Metamorphosis and The Rise and Fall of the Roman Empire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T11:28:59-07:00","id":1397775,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> I agree with your analysis of the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> that sounds like a pretty cool character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T12:37:36-07:00","id":1397791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397768#post1397768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm imagining a character who wants to compose <i>the</i> definitive historical account of the Usurpation, which I imagine is otherwise a complex, messy period that nobody has yet put in the work to investigate and make comprehensible.<br /> <br /> In gameplay terms, that largely amounts to investigating ruins and locating and interviewing knowledgeable figures, with actions to represent composing and recounting discrete portions in appropriate circumstances to get a desired reaction rather than actually track the full scope of the project.<br /> <br /> Something between Ovid's Metamorphosis and The Rise and Fall of the Roman Empire.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a DOPE campaign idea. You could even find some place where messed up savants weaponized Reality Engines so the outcome of the battle exists in three different versions, all simultaneously true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T17:53:22-07:00","id":1397864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397732#post1397732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh Please. What I mean is, after the Pearl Harbor is taken. <i>Afterward </i>the true battle for the Creation is commenced.<br /> <br /> And I have serious doubts about Usurpers capability to <i>assassinate </i>the Night Caste. I think they can counter Sidereals pretty well.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Solar charms do you feel make Solars immune to Sidereal/Dragonblooded assassins?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T01:54:00-07:00","id":1397922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397864#post1397864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What Solar charms do you feel make Solars immune to Sidereal/Dragonblooded assassins?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it is absurd that assassins assassinate an entire Caste of assassins?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T02:00:08-07:00","id":1397923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397922#post1397922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it is absurd that assassins assassinate an entire Caste of assassins?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah a whole cast of things taken down by their own method, I've probably never seen this in any litterature whatsoever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is a very strange proposal in terms of the exact timing it would require and the kind of Limit Break that would impair one's judgement sufficient to agree to such a task with such a vague appeal. </div> </div> </div>Take it the other way around : For a very important task, a Solar God-Invoker lends to one of his trusthworty friend the allegiance of a Third Circle Demon because he has to fight whatsoever monstrosity still exist in the First Age. He later receives a simple message telling him &quot;Do not finish your task yet. The time is soon to come.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not advocating it happened 100% (my position about the Usurpation is still it should be very broad and ill-defined to allow space for interpretation for different people), my position is if someone wanted to do the Usurpation I could totally see this happening.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T02:05:28-07:00","id":1397927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397922#post1397922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it is absurd that assassins assassinate an entire Caste of assassins?</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit I'm not a trained assassin but I wager that knowing how to be an assassin doesn't automatically mean you're an expert in how to counterattack all other forms of assassination. Like if you're a master of being overlooked and poisoning are you going to be able to locate a stealthed Air Aspect or an unassuming Sidereal before they make their strike? Like, one Air Aspect Charm lets the Dragonblood suck the breath out of someone's lungs. Assuming you are a living person who needs to breathe <i>that kind of shit is pretty debilitating</i>.<br /> <br /> And if you DO win, that's one victory. Next up is... Uh... The rest of the fucking army. And you're an assassin, not a warrior. You have shit endurance.<br /> <br /> Also they're technically YOUR troops but one of the commanders apparently told them &quot;The enemy is in the stronghold, burn it&quot; so you're trapped and they're watching the exits.<br /> <br /> Also also we'll just assume that you, a functioning person who lives in a society and likes to get along with other people, are <i>not</i> some construct of Late 2e Paranoia Combat whose skillset only includes Combat Charms and Surprise Negators, and you DON'T live in a habit of randomly killing someone who looks at you the wrong way, so you probably don't expect to be betrayed.<br /> <br /> Like, these aren't Random Enemies. That's Revaka, the Fire Aspect, he's been your lieutenant for a century. Guiding Star and you have apparently been friends for the past ten lifetimes. You <i>KNOW</i> these people. You're reasonably sure they won't kill you, and some of them you actively like or trust.<br /> <br /> To say nothing of how the Sidereals and the Dragonbloods, <i>not</i> being idiots, probably wouldn't try to kill a Solar in the way least likely to work. If you have Gleaming Edge of Destruction, a Dawn Caste, you're not gonna fight him head-on. Slip him some poison or play to his vices and strike when his guard is down.<br /> <br /> Whisper of Shadows is near-impossible to locate when she goes to ground or manages to hide, so instead find her safe houses, trap them. If she gets to one, it blows up, and the others were already raided, leaving her unable to resupply.<br /> <br /> Light of Brilliance, Sage and Artificer? Arrange a tragic lab accident, or just have the security be occupied and stab them since they're not a fighter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 06-21-2020, 05:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T02:16:07-07:00","id":1397930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397922#post1397922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it is absurd that assassins assassinate an entire Caste of assassins?</div> </div> </div> </div>*Laughs in <a href=\"https://www.thoughtco.com/history-of-the-assassins-hashshashin-195545\" target=\"_blank\">Mongolian</a>*<br /> *Laughs in <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=7kSuas6mRpk\" target=\"_blank\">Shogun Assassin</a>*<br /> *Laughs in <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=M6vtiaNqtv4\" target=\"_blank\">Seal Team Six</a>*<br /> *Laughs in <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=LK-uK5gOhYw\" target=\"_blank\">501st Legion</a>*<br /> *Laughs in <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=eNr0WXQ3Ho4\" target=\"_blank\">man-portable minigun</a>*<br /> *Laughs in <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=Ybw_vvyng4Y\" target=\"_blank\">Templar</a>*<br /> <br /> Assassins can be assassinated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 06-21-2020, 05:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T03:45:36-07:00","id":1397940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397922#post1397922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Because it is absurd that assassins assassinate an entire Caste of assassins? </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Your perspective both on the Night Caste and on the methods employed to try and kill them is reductive, and your line of reasoning is still faulty. It is not absurd in the least that Exalted specialized in assassination, and deeply immersed in a subculture that is being driven by it, should be outmanoeuvred and overcome.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Your lack of credibility for the Usurpation looks as though it is edging close to the territory of &quot;Solars Win&quot;.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397923#post1397923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take it the other way around : For a very important task, a Solar God-Invoker lends to one of his trusthworty friend the allegiance of a Third Circle Demon because he has to fight whatsoever monstrosity still exist in the First Age. He later receives a simple message telling him &quot;Do not finish your task yet. The time is soon to come.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand this, and I feel as though it is overlooking some things about how the spell &quot;Demon of the Third Circle&quot; works and what has typically been portrayed as the setting perspective on how perilous the unquestionable are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T04:09:46-07:00","id":1397944,"title":"","content":"This thread seems to consist of a series of people giving well-reasoned explanations for how the Usurpation occurred, only for the OP to reply with &quot;Nuh-uh, Solars are INVINCIBLE&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T04:16:27-07:00","id":1397947,"title":"","content":"The Usurpation happened. Mechanically, it is unlikely that it actually happened. Surely, we can concede that white-rooming a Calibration feast assassination is unlikely to see any Sidereal/Dragon-Blooded victory. We can say that it happened anyway without shouting down the young'un's who haven't read this thread that pops up every 8 months or so.<br /> <br /> Unlikely things happen all the time in Exalted. It's a collection of heroes overcoming the impossible, even other heroes, who meet tragic ends. Treachery, lies, preparation, misdirection, social influence, are worth more than top-tier combat Charms in the wonderfully messy Creation we call home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T04:28:37-07:00","id":1397949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397944#post1397944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread seems to consist of a series of people giving well-reasoned explanations for how the Usurpation occurred, only for the OP to reply with &quot;Nuh-uh, Solars are INVINCIBLE&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Please keep commentary to what people say versus commenting on the poster's response. Even if you disagree.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T04:57:58-07:00","id":1397953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397947#post1397947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Usurpation happened. Mechanically, it is unlikely that it actually happened. Surely, we can concede that white-rooming a Calibration feast assassination is unlikely to see any Sidereal/Dragon-Blooded victory. We can say that it happened anyway without shouting down the young'un's who haven't read this thread that pops up every 8 months or so.<br /> <br /> Unlikely things happen all the time in Exalted. It's a collection of heroes overcoming the impossible, even other heroes, who meet tragic ends. Treachery, lies, preparation, misdirection, social influence, are worth more than top-tier combat Charms in the wonderfully messy Creation we call home.</div> </div> </div> </div>The American Revolution was an unlikely to succeed event that succeeded. It took a great deal of things falling just so and conditions being just right, but it was an incredible feat against incredible odds. If it can happen in the real world then the best damn plotters in creation guided by Fate itself and backed with what amount to super spartans can overthrow beings that amount to Hercules, Odyssesus, Perseus etc. I see no real problem with this. Not disagreeing with you Tikor, I actually mean it as an agreement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T05:40:25-07:00","id":1397959,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t have anything new to offer, but I agree with all the well-reasoned arguments made by everyone else who explained how the Usurpation as written is definitely feasible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T06:19:38-07:00","id":1397971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397947#post1397947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanically, it is unlikely that it actually happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s this part that I\u2019m not convinced of. Sure, if everyone\u2019s built competently and they optimize their points and diversify their skills and never split the party and have sensible Intimacies and\u2026<br /> <br /> But that doesn\u2019t really seem like the kind of madness-stricken god-kings that the Sidereals would need to gather together over and ask each other, \u201cWhat\u2019s to be <i>done</i> about these petty, paranoid tyrants?\u201d <br /> <br /> And keep in mind, one of the most optimized-for-killing-large-quantities-of-DBs builds <i>ever</i> still went down to Dragon-Blooded blades after three successive white room fights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T09:27:17-07:00","id":1397992,"title":"","content":"I recall that optimized Solar was Essence 1? Without First Age Artifice and an army of dematerialized demons, and lacking Solar Sorcery and...<br /> <br /> I happen to think a combination of Solar solidarity and Investigation Charms would blow the cover of any conspiracy large enough to take them down, bringing swift, tyrannical retribution for uncovered thought-crimes. And even if every Solar somehow missed the signs, or were persuaded that other Solars were to blame, or found out and didn't tell their fellows, someone could Mind-Manse the clues together at Join Battle and lay out a case for solidarity then. A combination of AoE effects and a front-line/back-line rotation for Essence recoup, combined with many other tactical advantages of uniquely Solar making, and my money is on the Solars.<br /> <br /> Now, if you add the Lunars to the equation, I shift my bet. But that's not the Usurpation as written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T09:28:57-07:00","id":1397995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arkayriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397953#post1397953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The American Revolution was an unlikely to succeed event that succeeded. It took a great deal of things falling just so and conditions being just right, but it was an incredible feat against incredible odds. If it can happen in the real world then the best damn plotters in creation guided by Fate itself and backed with what amount to super spartans can overthrow beings that amount to Hercules, Odyssesus, Perseus etc. I see no real problem with this. Not disagreeing with you Tikor, I actually mean it as an agreement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, and good examples. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T09:35:13-07:00","id":1397997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397940#post1397940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand this, and I feel as though it is overlooking some things about how the spell &quot;Demon of the Third Circle&quot; works and what has typically been portrayed as the setting perspective on how perilous the unquestionable are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I want to keep argumenting this over too long posts so I'll try to do it very short : Use the summoning powers of the Solar against them in a scheme planned beforehand. I think the statement is broad enough that if you don't see how it could happen, you most likely do not agree with me that this could be done (which is fine with me).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T09:51:55-07:00","id":1397999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397992#post1397992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall that optimized Solar was Essence 1? Without First Age Artifice and an army of dematerialized demons, and lacking Solar Sorcery and...</div> </div> </div> </div>And once again, bringing a warstrider or an army of dematerialized demons to a fancy dress-up party <i>is bad form</i>. Does Arkansas Senator Tom Cotton carry an AR-15 with him to the Senate chambers for protection? No. The security's already being provided.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397992#post1397992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I happen to think a combination of Solar solidarity and Investigation Charms would blow the cover of any conspiracy large enough to take them down, bringing swift, tyrannical retribution for uncovered thought-crimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a person playing an Essence 4 Solar investigator, I happen to disagree.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T10:19:02-07:00","id":1398006,"title":"","content":"Sneaking an army into a party is less faux pas and more act of war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T10:29:28-07:00","id":1398009,"title":"","content":"I still think a big part of it is that most of the Solars probably didn't expect that they sould be betrayed. If they suspected an attack maybe they could have prepared. But most didn't because they didn't think to look for one.<br /> <br /> To use a weak metaphor, since Charms are just abstractions, many Charms require activation to use. And to uncover a conspiracy you gotta look for it.<br /> <br /> Now i'm willing to believe that maybe one Solar found out about the plan... And cue someone (maybe Thulio) appearing behind them and going &quot;Sorry, you know too much&quot; and them bleg, dead.<br /> <br /> The whole &quot;But why didn't the Solars rolfstomp them back?&quot; Is based on a lot of faulty assumptions. It assumes that a Solar staring down hundreds of Dragonbloods with even more mortal soldiers backing them up will laugh and slaughter them all. It assumes that every Solar knows Adamant Sorcery, or has a 5 dot Artifact weapon they've mastered the Evocations of. It assumes that they expected an attack and had a warstrider or something ready to launch at a moment's notice just in case something happens.<br /> <br /> It assumes that Solars are paranoid PCs who have the mindset of Doomsday preppers who stock an obscene amount of guns and baked beans rather than Solars having differing personalities and skillsets that are the result of their lives instead of being the result of Players building them with an idea of what's to come in mind.<br /> <br /> That's something to keep in mind. Characters in a game don't usually have access to the rulebook. And ultimately this talk is like trying to debate tactical outcomes from historical battles.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why didn't Whats-His-Face attack Those-Guys with a cavalry charge from their north flank and completely turn the tide?&quot;<br /> <br /> One could debate hypotheticals for a while about whether Whats-His-Face knew the flank was unprotected, what the conditions of the battle were like, if a cavalry charge was feasable or not, but ultimately trying to argue whether it could have gone another way boils down to &quot;And yet it happened this way&quot;<br /> <br /> Even when 2e spent most every book it could essentially mocking Dragonbloods for not being 'real' Exalts, especially compared to the great and grand Solars, the Usurpation happened. This is kinda something assumed for all Editions. Regardless of if it would happen or not with a bunch of bad assumptions, it still happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T10:41:12-07:00","id":1398014,"title":"","content":"Hmm... Yeah, to the extent the Usurpation could be said to be improbable via the mechanics for Second Age Solars that we have I would prefer the gap to bridged by.... &quot;Turns out late First Age Solar hubris is one hell of a dice penalty! In exactly this circumstance!&quot; over the usurpers simply lucking out and achieving something unlikely.<br /> <br /> Part of that is that the Path of Bronze is supposed to be the relatively safe* but lesser option. If it's actually the &quot;Kind of corner case probability-wise&quot; option that's not really much safer or more secure than the Path of Gold, then it doesn't really do what we're looking for.<br /> <br /> Some of the point of this aspect of the setting is that the Sidereals viewed it as more expedient and easier to usurp the Solars than try to persuade them and return them to virtue - and this is arguably a moral failing, or just and justified pragmatism, depending on where you're standing and how you roll play it out. So if the probabilities look like they're aligning the opposite way to any degree or align as equally probable, that's probably something to treat as &quot;limit to the resolution of the mechanics&quot;, rather than an objectively true thing in the setting where the Sidereals made a weird choice.<br /> <br /> *I mean, they're Solars, so relatively safe is still tough odds, but clearly very different to Path of Gold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T10:49:00-07:00","id":1398016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397992#post1397992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall that optimized Solar was Essence 1? Without First Age Artifice and an army of dematerialized demons, and lacking Solar Sorcery and...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was an Essence 1 Solar with a combat supernal, so higher essence mainly gives it more motes. So, send another 5 dragon blooded to get rid of the extra motes, plus 5 to deal with whatever essence 2+ non-supernal-ability charms they have. 25 dragon blooded is enough that you could send that many to attack every solar and still not be using the majority of dragon blooded. Most solars are not heavily optimized dragon blooded killers.<br /> Ignoring the things already mentioned about bringing warstriders and armies to a party - most First Age Artifice isn't better in a fight than regular artifacts (ie. clockwork birds, boats that don't sail on land, siege weapons, gunzosha armor [good in a fight for mortals, but not better than regular armor for Exalts). The attackers are exalts - many of them will be able to see and attack dematerialized demons.<br /> The optimized Solar who can kill 10+ dragonblooded alone makes heavy use of launching devastating strikes at the beginning of combat - Sorcery, especially Solar Sorcery, is often too slow. The only currently written solar circle sorcery spell useable in a fight is Death Ray, which is a fairly effect way to kill a handful of dragon blooded in a turn, and then have to survive a round without being crashed. Solars with Death Ray fall into the category of &quot;throw 20+dragonblooded at them and expect heavy casualties&quot;, but are far from unbeatable. During the main fight at Calibration you could hit more than a handful, but would also hit a handful of solars. Also, killing a DB in one hit with Death Ray is possible, but not guaranteed - rolling 13 dice, with 6 successes from the spell and willpower is an average of 12.5 successes. An optimized DB has a defense of 6+1(melee weapon)+3(excellency)+1(willpower)+1(stunt) = 12, so you may or may not hit. Damage is initiative (6 might be normal, 9.5 optimized no excellency, 14.5 optimized excellency, 16.8 for awakening eye and a willpower)+extra successes (1-ish)+current temporary willpower (10, -1 for casting the spell, -1 for spending one on the attack) = somewhere from 14 to 30, so 6 to 12 levels of damage. Ox-bodies and resistance charms will cover that. The second and third round are better, especially since the DB can't keep spending 6m, 1wp on defense indefinitely, but also give more time for someone to kill or crash you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T11:02:54-07:00","id":1398020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397922#post1397922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it is absurd that assassins assassinate an entire Caste of assassins?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it likewise absurd that warriors kill an entire caste of warriors in a war? Also remember here, only Dawns have combat caste abilities, whereas every single DB Aspect has a combat ability, and 3/5ths of the Sidereal castes have one as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397992#post1397992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall that optimized Solar was Essence 1? Without First Age Artifice and an army of dematerialized demons, and lacking Solar Sorcery and...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but who do you think is running the first age artiface? Who were the commanders in charge of the Thousand Forged Dragon silos? On the Directional Titans there might be one Eclipse captain, a Twilight sorcerer-engineer, and 80 terrestrial soldiers and savants. Once they take care of their commanders, that's the rebel's Directional Titan now.<br /> <br /> Also before taking stuff from the Solars the Sidereals and Terrestrirals also had first age artiface already. A Solar general wearing first-age power armor isn't fighting his lieutenants in a mish-mash of mundane weapons and a sprinkling of artifacts, he's fighting his lieutenants wearing Dragon Armor and wielding firelances and implosion bows.<br /> <br /> Even the armies of dematerialized demons, sure a Twilight can summon a lot, but compare how many demons a Twilight can summon compared to ten Dragonblooded and a Sidereal, the Twilight gets out-summoned real quick. The only thing they have that the rebels don't is that a small sliver of Solar sorcerers are powerful and daring enough to summon third circle demons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397992#post1397992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I happen to think a combination of Solar solidarity and Investigation Charms would blow the cover of any conspiracy large enough to take them down, bringing swift, tyrannical retribution for uncovered thought-crimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since we're talking about third edition and mechanics, what charms specifically make it impossible for a Solar to fail to notice what's going on? There's some really good ones, like Ten Magistrate Eyes, but there's some pretty good terrestrial larceny charms too, like Infallible Alibi Approach, which lets you reflexively roll to dissolve evidence into water with your full pool and double 7s.<br /> <br /> Even if a Solar investigator did manage to make the connection to what was going on, they would then have to contact and convince the rest of the Solars about this, and do so without suffering an unfortunate accident first. Normally that might be next to impossible, but for Sidereal fate-ninjas it would only be very hard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397992#post1397992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And even if every Solar somehow missed the signs, or were persuaded that other Solars were to blame, or found out and didn't tell their fellows, someone could Mind-Manse the clues together at Join Battle and lay out a case for solidarity then.</div> </div> </div> </div>The moment that Solar uses Mind-Manse Meditation she's dead. It makes you completely unaware of your surroundings for the duration so while she's putting together all the tiny fragments of why the hell the guards of the banquet have started stabbing people she's completely defenseless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397992#post1397992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A combination of AoE effects and a front-line/back-line rotation for Essence recoup, combined with many other tactical advantages of uniquely Solar making, and my money is on the Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those tactics work better for the rebels than they work for the Solars.<br /> <br /> Remember, they're all at the calibration feast, if the rebels detonate a massive explosion that takes out the floor and drops all the feasters down a level amid shards of broken stone, you just hit 100% of the Solars with that assault. They're also surrounded by rebel forces, so you can fire off a Death of Obsidian Butterflies out the side and deal a little pie slice of damage to the dragons, but they can drop an Arrow Rain Tempest right on the middle of the Solars and hit everyone again.<br /> <br /> That also makes front-back line rotation almost impossible. You're either in the front line crossing blades with the Melee/Brawl/MAist Dragonblooded, or you're in the middle getting pelted by the archery/thrown/sorcery dragonblooded. Not to mention that with a large number of Solars barely being warriors at all, a huge number will get cut down right at the start, and shrink the size of the embattled Solars a lot.<br /> <br /> Also, animas. We're talking mechanics right? When a Solar gets crashed and loses her hardness, every single bonfire terrestiral anima within Close range is going to hit her with decisive damage, poison, and a knockdown effect. The fire aspects will also be dealing additional damage. Basically, you get crashed, you die before your next turn.<br /> <br /> That's if you're wearing artifact armor or something else that gives you scenelong Hardness by the way. If you don't have scenelong hardness the Dragonblooded may not even bother attacking you, their animas will crash you and then kill you all on their own.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T11:10:48-07:00","id":1398022,"title":"","content":"There's basically two things you need to consider.<br /> <br /> 1) The usurpation happened<br /> <br /> 2) the usurpation is not described in very much detail in 3E.<br /> <br /> So, like, what do you think <i>would</i> need to happen to make it plausible?<br /> <br /> Whatever you come up with, that's how it happened in your canon.<br /> <br /> Think it needs some traitor solars who helped hide the plans thinking they'd be able to rule the world without rivals? Then there were some. Think it needs some secret sidereal superweapon? Boom, there you go.<br /> <br /> Don't go in thinking &quot;this was clearly impossible&quot; cos it obviously wasn't. Just... come up with something. Or don't. It doesn't actually matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T12:47:33-07:00","id":1398043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1398022#post1398022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's basically two things you need to consider.<br /> <br /> 1) The usurpation happened<br /> <br /> 2) the usurpation is not described in very much detail in 3E.<br /> <br /> So, like, what do you think <i>would</i> need to happen to make it plausible?<br /> <br /> Whatever you come up with, that's how it happened in your canon.<br /> <br /> Think it needs some traitor solars who helped hide the plans thinking they'd be able to rule the world without rivals? Then there were some. Think it needs some secret sidereal superweapon? Boom, there you go.<br /> <br /> Don't go in thinking &quot;this was clearly impossible&quot; cos it obviously wasn't. Just... come up with something. Or don't. It doesn't actually matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Thank you ! I very much like the idea of Solar traitors participating in their downfall by the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T13:04:25-07:00","id":1398045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1398020#post1398020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3/5ths of the Sidereal castes have [a combat Caste Ability] as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, wasn't the last dev statement about Sidereal Ability spreads that all of them would get Martial Arts as a Caste Ability?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T13:12:32-07:00","id":1398047,"title":"","content":"Canonically, the Usurpation happened. No one here is going to convince the dev team to preface future books with &quot;haha the Usurpation never actually happened, j/k, we're rewriting the backstory of the setting to get rid of it.&quot; So I'm unclear on the intended purpose of this thread.<br /> <br /> If the idea is to find a way to make the Usurpation work, then a few dozen informative replies are enough to either put together something satisfactory for your game, or to determine that you just can't work with it.<br /> <br /> If the idea is that the Usurpation axiomatically doesn't work \u2014 or if that's the conclusion drawn as per the previous note about not finding anything satisfactory in the thread \u2014 then it's time to start a new thread about how best to run an alternate-timeline game in which the Usurpation never happened. This is a fruitful topic for discussion!<br /> <br /> I don't see the point of harping on a disagreement with canon without either working to find common ground, or else shifting gears into a homebrew approach. It seems unproductive to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T13:27:56-07:00","id":1398050,"title":"","content":"The Usurpation is improbable mechanically because <i>the mechanics aren't built to model dozens of Celestial and hundreds of Terrestrial Exalted all mashed together in a horrific scrum</i>.<br /> <br /> The setting is bigger than what takes place in your games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T16:31:16-07:00","id":1398081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397992#post1397992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall that optimized Solar was Essence 1? Without First Age Artifice and an army of dematerialized demons, and lacking Solar Sorcery and...</div> </div> </div> </div>You wound me.<br /> <br /> Essence 5 Twilight with every (Corebook) Essence 4 and lower Charm in every Ability. Artifact weapon and armor.<br /> <br /> I mean, sure, you could push harder. But optimized to the hilt with every Essence 5 Charm, Evocations and Sorcery... I still don't see you getting above 30 DBs. And that's using Ahlat as a stand-in for your 3CD.<br /> <br /> The mote economy just isn't there. The days of Infinite (Dragon-Blooded) Mastery are gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T17:11:45-07:00","id":1398085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1398047#post1398047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm unclear on the intended purpose of this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>The purpose, as I read it, is to mentally, mechanically occupy a storied moment of the setting history. For funsies. <br /> <br /> Sure, each table will accept or reject the Usurpation, like any parcel of canon. Armchair-generalling old battles in old wars, especially pivotal ones, is a past-time that any storied historical combat cannot escape, real or imagined.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T17:12:20-07:00","id":1398086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1398081#post1398081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You wound me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies. I must have been thinking of another fight.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T17:15:24-07:00","id":1398088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1398020#post1398020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The moment that Solar uses Mind-Manse Meditation she's dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Defend Other.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T18:01:32-07:00","id":1398091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1398050#post1398050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Usurpation is improbable mechanically because <i>the mechanics aren't built to model dozens of Celestial and hundreds of Terrestrial Exalted all mashed together in a horrific scrum</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I very much agree with this vis a vis the Calibration feast. To add a different phrasing of I think the same idea: mechanically, a battle including dozens to hundreds of exalts on both sides will hinge heavily on effects which can effect an indefinite number of people without concern for friendly fire. This is probably not an accurate measure of the setting, so should probably be taken as meaning the mechanics are designed around the middle, and reach odd conclusions at the extremes. Because of this, it probably isn't helpful to consider the precise unreasonable outcomes of the mechanics.<br /> <br /> But that leaves me nothing to do, so I'll instead switch from considering AoE attacks to friendly AoEs. <br /> <br /> Battle Anthem of the Ten Thousand Dragons: Possibly Team DB only, but a single loyalist DB knowing the charm could grant it to the Solars. Grants 1 free die to attack rolls, movement, and command actions. Allied battlegroups get a die to resist rout. Successful withering attacks grant 1 bonus point of initiative.<br /> Battle Anthem of the Lunar Exalted: Probably Team Solar only. Bonus die to attack rolls. Rage based intimacies count as 1 level higher. Battlegroups get lower of (essence or performance) dice to attacks and rout checks.<br /> Battle Anthem of the Solar Exalted: Probably Team Solar only. Grants 1i per round, allied battlegroups gain (essence) dice to attacks. Soul Voice increases this to 2i, and (essence) successes<br /> Soul-Stirring Cantata: Probably Team Solar only. Grants 1m/round, doubled by Soul Voice.<br /> Heroism-Encouraging Ballad: Probably Team Solar only. Double intimacy bonuses against fear. Allied battlegroups gain (essence) successes to rally for numbers.<br /> Inspiring Battle Hymn: Both teams can probably have this. Reroll 1s on join battle, +1 resolve against fear.<br /> Aria of Victory: Both teams can probably have this, Team DB may be inhibited by the Terrestrial keyword. Grants 1 willpower each turn, which lasts for that turn and possibly cannot be spent on charms. Terrestrial forces you to commit 4m/turn, but who cares, one terrestrial losing a bunch of motes is pretty small compared to the melee supernal killing 5 people/turn over there.<br /> <br /> All of these rely on you being heard, which possibly means they don't actually affect everyone in the battle.<br /> Maybe you can use noise-enhancing charms, but presumably those don't work if everyone is using them.<br /> Actually, how many of the survivors of the Usurpation had hearing loss from it?<br /> <br /> Any social influence charms could qualify, really. Spend a bunch of motes on your roll, force every enemy you can communicate with to either spend motes resisting, or willpower. <br /> <br /> Even if shouting as loudly as you can is useless because any influence is drowned out by everyone else's shouting, it's still useful to deny your enemy coordination/willpower removal by drowning them out. Telepathy charms are great for this.<br /> <br /> Seems like the solar wide area of charms will beat out the dragon blooded battle anthem, except I'm probably missing a handful of charms. I would worry that Team DB can more afford to have 10 people stand to the side singing than Team Solar can.<br /> <br /> From this I (sarcastically) conclude that the Usurpation included several dozen Dragonblooded shouting encouragements, threats, requests for surrender, tactical advice, etc at superhuman volumes and/or inside people's minds, as well as a handful of Solars doing the same for the other side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T20:40:02-07:00","id":1398109,"title":"","content":"Isn't there a canon example of a Solar getting their shit riggity-wrecked by a group of mortal soldiers, specifically because the Solar:<br /> <br /> 1) Underestimated the mortals<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> 2) Overestimated their own abilities?<br /> <br /> I distinctly remember something along those lines being a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T20:51:30-07:00","id":1398112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1398109#post1398109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't there a canon example of a Solar getting their shit riggity-wrecked by a group of mortal soldiers, specifically because the Solar:<br /> <br /> 1) Underestimated the mortals<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> 2) Overestimated their own abilities?<br /> <br /> I distinctly remember something along those lines being a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno about it happening in canon (it may have but I don't recall it specifically at the moment) but it <i>definitely </i>happened in my seafaring game. He also 3) Was standing on a lifeboat out on the open ocean and wearing heavy armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T20:57:28-07:00","id":1398114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1398112#post1398112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He also was standing on a lifeboat out on the open ocean and wearing heavy armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah, classic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T21:15:17-07:00","id":1398118,"title":"","content":"The only part of the Usurpation that strains credulity for me is keeping it secret in advance despite the scale of moobilization. That\u2019s why my go to answer is that the Breaking of the Mask happened before the Usurpation as a reality breaking work of astrology specifically toward that end. In theory a majority of Sidereals together can pull off other reality breaking works of astrology breaking other constellations, though every time weakens the Loom and reality and that breaking has permanent consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T21:54:07-07:00","id":1398122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1398118#post1398118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only part of the Usurpation that strains credulity for me is keeping it secret in advance despite the scale of moobilization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, though, only the people at the top of the conspiracy pyramid are generally even told that there's a conspiracy.<br /> <br /> It's one of the reasons why (to pick an obvious example) QAnon is horseshit; if Donald Trump <i>really was</i> a <b>secret </b>tactical genius working hard to expose a cabal of deep-state Jewish Satanist pedophiles by going deep cover <i>appearing to be</i> a racist incompetent loser mired in corruption and sex crime allegations, highly-placed loyal people in his administration <i>would not be disseminating it</i> to people on 4chan.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf the troops need to be moved in order to murder the Solars, they'll be given a reason that's not &quot;We're gonna have you murder the Solars.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200b(For an example that's admittedly smaller-scale, you might look at the time the moderate leadership of the NRA was usurped and replaced by the group of trigger-happy nut-jobs that have held it to this day.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-22-2020, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T22:18:00-07:00","id":1398123,"title":"","content":"Also by using nested catspaws you shut down a whole hell of a lot of Solar investigation &quot;I win&quot; charm magic. Like if the people that you're telling to do a thing don't even know they're being traitors while they're doing it, none of those charms that do things like feel the intent of the character as they were doing a particular action will come up with very useful information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T22:23:24-07:00","id":1398124,"title":"","content":"While we're on the subject of catspaws, yes, the list of best counters to Judge's Ear Technique includes &quot;the speaker is not aware that what he's saying isn't true.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>That said,</b> don't underestimate &quot;the lie is so comfortable that the investigator doesn't <i>want </i>to look into whether it's true or not,&quot; or &quot;the truth is so ugly that the investigator rules it out for her peace of mind.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-22-2020, 01:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T02:41:24-07:00","id":1398143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1398109#post1398109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't there a canon example of a Solar getting their shit riggity-wrecked by a group of mortal soldiers, specifically because the Solar:<br /> <br /> 1) Underestimated the mortals<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> 2) Overestimated their own abilities?<br /> <br /> I distinctly remember something along those lines being a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Suddenly I'm imagining things in terms of a lengthy social engagement involving lots of Solars being a thing in which they might not only be heavy with food and fuzzy with drink, but where a decent amount of Essence has been expended throughout things like their interpersonal interactions and trying to impress one another, perhaps egged on a bit by attendant Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't break such a thing down quantitatively, but it's a perspective on how Solars might not go into every situation running on a full tank, which would seem like the kind of thing to value tactically against them in any case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T02:47:47-07:00","id":1398145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1398109#post1398109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't there a canon example of a Solar getting their shit riggity-wrecked by a group of mortal soldiers, specifically because the Solar:<br /> <br /> 1) Underestimated the mortals<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> 2) Overestimated their own abilities?<br /> <br /> I distinctly remember something along those lines being a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>In <i>Tale of the Visiting Flare</i>, the pre-Incarnation of the Solar hero was killed more or less Torches and Pitchforks style by a mob whipped into frenzy by an Exalted stalker. And this was apparently <i>The</i>Dawn when it came to Evocations, so much that people never stopped hounding him to show them what their artifacts could do. <br /> <br /> I don't remember if it was specifically that he was a haughty jackass or that he was just drown in bodies, but their you go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T05:39:49-07:00","id":1398164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1398143#post1398143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suddenly I'm imagining things in terms of a lengthy social engagement involving lots of Solars being a thing in which they might not only be heavy with food and fuzzy with drink, but where a decent amount of Essence has been expended throughout things like their interpersonal interactions and trying to impress one another, perhaps egged on a bit by attendant Dragon.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s another thing you could use cats paws for, even. Tell the aid of one of the Solar athletes that you heard one of his rivals has surpassed him in strength and everyone is talking about it. Now that aid earnestly suggests that a legendary Nine Aeons Thews level arm wrestle take place to prove nobody surpassed anything. With all the big Solar performance, presence, and socialize stuff flying around you\u2019ll also have lots of people spending willpower just to not have their intimacies come out of Calibration all messed up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T06:09:46-07:00","id":1398169,"title":"","content":"Oh also. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397992#post1397992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I happen to think a combination of Solar solidarity</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably something that was pretty thin on the ground. This whole thing came to a head because the Solar Exalted were slowly losing their minds and endangering the world in the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 06-22-2020, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T06:38:14-07:00","id":1398174,"title":"","content":"The wonderful thing about 3e is it doesn't try to nail down the Usurpation for us, instead telling us to try and imagine what happened for ourselves. The fact that we have no hard facts means we're free to assume that things happened that history never recorded. Perhaps in Nara-O's Big Ol' Book of Secrets-n-Stuff is a tale of the greatest Night Caste to ever have lived. A night caste who disgusted with the decadence and madness he saw around him decided to do something about it. Maybe he worked with the Sidereals even agreeing to have his own essence sealed away when things were over to remove the Solar menace from existence forever. Or maybe he pulled a Rakan Thulio and manipulated his fellow Solars while never letting the Sidereals know he was on their side. Numinous asked how a caste of assassins could have been assassinated and others wondered how the secret could have been kept. Maybe the individual most trusted to ferret out the enemies of the Solars manipulated them into never seeing the threat until it was too late. This is all apart of my personal head cannon of course, but I think traitors amongst the Solars and Lunars is a feasible possibilty that we ignore because it's never been stated. Well much about the Usurpation is a mystery and if no one discovered the traitors or it's being held as a super tightly guarded secret we wouldn't know. I still think it's another possibility to consider when you're trying to simply wrap your head around how the Usurpation could have possibly happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T07:45:38-07:00","id":1398180,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s certainly possible there were Solar conspirators, either fully on board ones or maybe even ones who had no idea the ultimate goal of the plan was to deal away all Solars including them. I do think it\u2019s bad for everyone involved to say that there MUST have been Solar conspirators for it to happen though. It\u2019s bad for the rebels for obvious reasons, since its saying that the only Exalted who can actually punch up and do the impossible are Solars, and everyone else needs to remember their place, the only people who ever get to beat Solars are Solars.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s even bad for Solars, since any victory they gain isn\u2019t through determination, hard/dangerous work, or daring, it was always just inevitable. Solar warriors aren\u2019t brave, because they never risk anything, because they can\u2019t lose. Solar engineers who built the Sword of Creation didn\u2019t labor for centuries leveraging the greatest mortal civilization in history to make a worldwide defence network, that was just a Tuesday for them. Solar magistrates don\u2019t bravely delve into the criminal underworld, risking their lives and tapping every resource they have to ferret out corruption, they just see everything and instantly jump to the right conclusion without fail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T08:04:52-07:00","id":1398182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1398180#post1398180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s certainly possible there were Solar conspirators, either fully on board ones or maybe even ones who had no idea the ultimate goal of the plan was to deal away all Solars including them. I do think it\u2019s bad for everyone involved to say that there MUST have been Solar conspirators for it to happen though. It\u2019s bad for the rebels for obvious reasons, since its saying that the only Exalted who can actually punch up and do the impossible are Solars, and everyone else needs to remember their place, the only people who ever get to beat Solars are Solars.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s even bad for Solars, since any victory they gain isn\u2019t through determination, hard/dangerous work, or daring, it was always just inevitable. Solar warriors aren\u2019t brave, because they never risk anything, because they can\u2019t lose. Solar engineers who built the Sword of Creation didn\u2019t labor for centuries leveraging the greatest mortal civilization in history to make a worldwide defence network, that was just a Tuesday for them. Solar magistrates don\u2019t bravely delve into the criminal underworld, risking their lives and tapping every resource they have to ferret out corruption, they just see everything and instantly jump to the right conclusion without fail.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True. I merely want to point out more reasons it could have happened. For instance Solars were beings who became immensely powerful. Immensely powerful beings often become complacent. Complacent tyrants often get shanked.<br /> <br /> I'm pointing out that because we know so little it should be easier, not harder to imagine the Usurpation as possible. Numinous can doubt what we say, we can rebut the doubts raised, but in the end we're just spitting out opinions on how it was possible or why it wasn't. The only fact we know is it happened, and so if we're going to help Numinous with gaining credibilty with something that is a fact of the setting we need as many reasons as possible. While I like the traitor theory of mine, I'm in no way meaning that it's what must have happened. Personally I favor arrogant complacency combined with characters built like real people, and not players wanting to curb stomp every danger in existence 3 seconds before it happens even though they're the diplomat, as the biggest reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","user":"Arkayriel","date":". 06-22-2020, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T09:01:55-07:00","id":1398190,"title":"","content":"Kinda depends how many layers deep you go. <br /> <br /> &quot;The usurpation would have been impossible without solar turncoats helping&quot; is bad, but &quot;The conspirators tricked some solars into aiding their cause through promises of wealth and power and then backstabbed them when their jobs were done&quot; feels like the Sidereals and Dragon Blooded are back in the drivers seat again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T09:47:46-07:00","id":1398195,"title":"","content":"Also, seems a very Sidereal kind of plan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T10:15:49-07:00","id":1398196,"title":"","content":"Very true.<br /> <br /> Even just as a possibility that it was all a Solar plot is fine, but I\u2019ve seen people go so far as to say that the Scarlet Empress can\u2019t be a terrestrial, because she and her circle made it through the Imperial Manse and then she set up a global superpower, and thus must be a Usurpation survivor in disguise. Which explains why she doesn\u2019t seem to age, and also how she can treat with the Sidereals on a somewhat equal footing, and how she can keep herself in charge of her dynasty.<br /> <br /> Cool idea, nice alternate Creation for a particular campaign. It just shouldn\u2019t be unbelievable that a terrestrial made herself empress, but a Solar making themselves empress while masquerading as a DB including birthing a dynasty of DBs, and fooling even elder Secrets caste Sidereals is such a simple matter that it requires no further explanation and must be what\u2019s actually happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T10:54:37-07:00","id":1398199,"title":"","content":"If you want to delve into Solars killing each other during the Usurpation, secret conspiracies and Sidereal betrayals are all well and good, but they're also not strictly necessary. Just take the Solars who already hated each other and give them a little push. First Age Solars weren't a tight-knit family who all loved each other. Solars' rivals and enemies were at least as likely to be Solars as anyone else, and a key role of an organization like the Second Deliberative would have been to make sure that the Exalted stopped wrecking the place with their duels and wars against each other \u2014 or at least toned it down a bit to cut back on collateral damage.<br /> <br /> More specifically, the literal point of the Calibration Feast was that Solars attended not just to demonstrate that they weren't summoning Third Circle demons, but because <i>they didn't trust their fellows </i>who said they weren't summoning Third Circle demons. Whatever social purposes it eventually came to serve, at its root was a gathering for Solars who distrusted Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T11:11:50-07:00","id":1398201,"title":"","content":"Weren't there like a million DB's at the time? No amount of Solar Charms, especially with the slightly lower powerlevels of 3e, are going to be help much against a literal <i>nation</i> of elemental warriors ambushing you with the help of 100 fate ninjas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T11:27:29-07:00","id":1398204,"title":"","content":"Version of the Usurpation that are heavily reliant on formented conflict between Solars, are not wrong... but I would tend not to go with them.<br /> <br /> For why, again this gets back to looking at what the Usurpation is supposed to be, in its themes - for me, and I think this is borne out by the descriptions we get in memories of past lives, it's an event where the Solars were challenged, and their world order and legitimacy openly rejected by their lessers (by a &quot;class&quot; that they thought were beneath them), and they were openly cast down, righteously or with great injustice (depending on the perspective).<br /> <br /> This leaves memories which echo through their future incarnations and then inform to some extent characters in play in the Age of Sorrows. This is the most useful purpose for Exalted that I can think of, for actually describing how the Usurpation and Calibration Feast ambush actually happened.<br /> <br /> So if you change this to a situation where as far as the Solars have deep memories, it was of an event more like a sudden civil war between the Solars themselves, for me, it just doesn't serve that purpose as well.<br /> <br /> Leaning too far on the Usurpation as occured via incited conflict between Solars (or even more so, reducing to a Solar scheme that got out of control!), then, is neither necessary, nor, for me, the best way to milk the situation for what it's most worth for drama in the Age of Sorrows. Solars not coordinating with each other at all - that's a rich part of that situation, of course, but actual warfare between Solar participants, something different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T11:41:39-07:00","id":1398210,"title":"","content":"To steal an analogy from American politics, Democrats and Republicans will spend years undermining each other in speeches, advertisements, votes, and any other means at their disposal. <br /> <br /> But the elite of each party will still stand together, having a ruling-class solidarity against anyone trying to take their power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T12:02:54-07:00","id":1398215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1398047#post1398047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Canonically, the Usurpation happened. No one here is going to convince the dev team to preface future books with &quot;haha the Usurpation never actually happened, j/k, we're rewriting the backstory of the setting to get rid of it.&quot; So I'm unclear on the intended purpose of this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be funny to imagine the authors of pretty much any fictional setting being convinced that the story doesn't logically make sense and therefore retracting it, like Frege stopping the presses on <i>Grundgesetze der Arithmetik </i>after Russell found a contradiction in his axioms. (Which itself isn't quite what happened...)<br /> <br /> It also seems relevant to point out that, if the United States passed a constitutional amendment carving out an exception to the First Amendment for RPG settings with inconsistent backstories, and a law barring the publication of such RPGs, and then some brave forum poster managed to convince a judge that the Usurpation doesn't really make sense when you think about it, the solution would not be to redesign Exalted to avoid the Usurpation (cool though that alternate history might be), but rather to <i>make the Solars a little bit less powerful. </i>Or make the DBs a little more powerful. Either one would preserve most of the history, locations, and generally things people like about Exalted, rather than removing the Usurpation, which would upend basically all of it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T12:14:08-07:00","id":1398216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1398210#post1398210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To steal an analogy from American politics, Democrats and Republicans will spend years undermining each other in speeches, advertisements, votes, and any other means at their disposal.<br /> <br /> But the elite of each party will still stand together, having a ruling-class solidarity against anyone trying to take their power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell it to Aaron Burr.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, this is a fundamentally flawed analogy because it presents the First Age as a unified world government, which is not how it's presented in 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":1120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","user":"Eric Minton","date":". 06-22-2020, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T12:18:56-07:00","id":1398217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1398204#post1398204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Version of the Usurpation that are heavily reliant on formented conflict between Solars, are not wrong... but I would tend not to go with them.<br /> <br /> For why, again this gets back to looking at what the Usurpation is supposed to be, in its themes - for me, and I think this is borne out by the descriptions we get in memories of past lives, it's an event where the Solars were challenged, and their world order and legitimacy openly rejected by their lessers (by a &quot;class&quot; that they thought were beneath them), and they were openly cast down, righteously or with great injustice (depending on the perspective).<br /> <br /> This leaves memories which echo through their future incarnations and then inform to some extent characters in play in the Age of Sorrows. This is the most useful purpose for Exalted that I can think of, for actually describing how the Usurpation and Calibration Feast ambush actually happened.<br /> <br /> So if you change this to a situation where as far as the Solars have deep memories, it was of an event more like a sudden civil war between the Solars themselves, for me, it just doesn't serve that purpose as well.<br /> <br /> Leaning too far on the Usurpation as occured via incited conflict between Solars (or even more so, reducing to a Solar scheme that got out of control!), then, is neither necessary, nor, for me, the best way to milk the situation for what it's most worth for drama in the Age of Sorrows. Solars not coordinating with each other at all - that's a rich part of that situation, of course, but actual warfare between Solar participants, something different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that discussion of the nitty-gritty of the Usurpation (which, by and large<i>, </i><i>does not matter</i> in the Age of Sorrows) should revolve around conflicts between Solars. But if folks are going to delve into that nitty-gritty, I don't think it's helpful to erase those conflicts either \u2014 especially because players tend to project discussion of First Age Solars forward into Age of Sorrows actual play. It's totally legitimate for your modern-day Solar PC to issue calls of unity to her peers in the name of the friendship and harmony the Solar Host shared in the First Age, but like all such calls to the utopias of yesteryear, the historical record will not bear it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T12:50:07-07:00","id":1398224,"title":"","content":"Absolutely. And on the Sidereal and Dragonblooded side of the ledger, a bit of the same too (though I would assume they were a *bit* more unified).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T14:41:59-07:00","id":1398239,"title":"","content":"I think, we still think of Solars and Lunars as a hivemind. As if they would decide to act as a block. They had a society, but they were (extraordinary) individuals, with passions and epic goals. Even more so with the Great Curse on. The Sidereals are not battle-planners and generals to the usurpation war, they are also adept of intrigue, very well-informed and very patient, with long time to plan. They know which buttons to press, on the DBs and the Solars. <br /> <br /> I purpose - what if the usurpers turned some powerful solars on the Usurpation side? There are many ways to accomplish that, be it Justice (the solars are destroying creation! And we can prove), Pride (Can you accept your banishment quietly? We can give you an army, go and take control!), Crazy (We will help make everything burn! Show them the beautiful deaths you so want), and so on. Throw in some Lunars, as well! <br /> <br /> Having solars could help hide things up, and help turn the tide of combat. It would only a matter of betraying and killing the tired solars who remained or cleaning up much later. Where did the solar exaltations that kept exalting come from? Perhaps they are the few that helped turn the tide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T19:09:49-07:00","id":1398270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1398201#post1398201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weren't there like a million DB's at the time? No amount of Solar Charms, especially with the slightly lower powerlevels of 3e, are going to be help much against a literal <i>nation</i> of elemental warriors ambushing you with the help of 100 fate ninjas.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2e yes. In 1e and 3e it's never said, but the setting seems built on the idea that DBs are indivdiually powerful enough you don't need a million of them to be a world-dominating threat. The numbers we have in the world today are sufficient for a lot of their accomplishments, and the differences in the First Age for their base probably was more available equipment than raw numbers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T19:55:21-07:00","id":1398278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1397992#post1397992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall that optimized Solar was Essence 1? Without First Age Artifice and an army of dematerialized demons, and lacking Solar Sorcery and...</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha no. You are thinking of Shining Topaz. E1 Dawn. And Topaz goes down hard to the second wave of DBs, since when she vaporized the wyld hunt it took all her motes and almost all her wp.<br /> <br /> The actual optimized solar was like E5 with every charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T05:00:46-07:00","id":1398333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397447-success-of-the-usurpation?p=1398216#post1398216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tell it to Aaron Burr.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you had to choose...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T17:28:19-07:00","id":1398666,"title":"","content":"Oh, actually, I want to field the question of whether or not the First Age should or could have had a meaningfully greater number of Dragon Blooded, because I've remembered some things.<br /> <br /> My answer would be &quot;yes, obviously&quot;... if one assumes that the overall world population was much greater than it is at the Time of Tumult.<br /> <br /> We can see what the outcaste numbers that arise from the population of Creation are in the census. If I opt to count in a sizable number of patricians (on the assumption that their bloodlines are often no better than any lower class mortal) and a decent number of Lookshy (which has always been presented as absorbing most of the outcaste population of the Scavenger Lands), we get somewhere between ten and eleven thousand. I feel safe in assuming that the vast majority of outcastes are not the result of tiny little bloodlines maintaining themselves or the children of more well-bred Exalts, and are instead the unlikely occasion of the tiniest trickles of the Dragon's Blood emerging into true Exaltation.<br /> <br /> I would contend that in a much larger population, the ratio remains consistent. I would even argue that if you got a much higher proportion of the Dragon Blooded population not being too hung up on ensuring the strength of their own bloodlines, it would actually go up a bit.<br /> <br /> This leads into my proposal that throughout much of the First Age, the overall Dragon Blooded population was high enough that many Dragon Blooded didn't feel a need to be so hung up, feeding back into a loop where they have children among whomever and maintain a constant distribution of the progenitive Essence throughout the world's overall population. That and cases where they leverage the heredity of their power into marriage among mortal potentates in a manner that has results much like the royalty of Iscomay; sure you're not likely to have the very next heir by Exalted, but you're introducing a factor that might be expected to produce Exaltation every few generations, and that's a lot better than you had before.<br /> <br /> That complements a perspective that through much of the First Age, distributions of loyalty throughout and sense of duty to the Realm were something other than obligations to a family line. In this Edition, not necessarily loyalty to a Solar, but loyalty to <i>something</i> other than your immediate and extended family members. Perhaps a much greater emphasis on what the Scarlet Realm will eventually call Lost Eggs and the Kinships that they form to pursue their agendas (although I imagine even greater institutions beyond that in which Terrestrial Exalted advance on their personal merits and the bonds that they form on their own initiatives).<br /> <br /> It's still a system where I imagine that some highly concentrated bloodlines of consistent Exalted exist, but by the Terrestrials at large they're viewed somewhere between insular oddities and a slightly odious necessity in being absolutely sure that their kind will consistently pop up. They don't necessarily have any greater property or power than the rest do (helped by decoupling breeding from mote pools and Charm minimums), although a great many of them feel as though they should. Among a lot of those types is a level of pride in their pedigree and traceable heritage back to the most ancient heroes that a lot of their contemporaries view as quaint and pitiful.<br /> <br /> My conception of the lead up to the Usurpation is one in which a great many Exalted become increasingly frustrated with growing liberties of the Solar and Lunar Exalted, an increasing accumulation of power in their own hands (particularly if many of them see their greater distribution and activity as the real things that make the Realm), and in response to this a lot more of them cluster together and ultimately adopt a lot of the practices and outlook of the old clannish types. From this environment emerges a lot of the perspective that dominion over all Creation is theirs by right, they become increasingly defensive and aristocratic about it, and this is the impulse that Sidereals can target to encourage them to ultimately seize the reins of the world.<br /> <br /> In this schema, I perceive that there was a time when Terrestrial Exalted was the norm as the term they used for themselves. Dragon Blooded becomes in vogue when their attitude shifts towards more emphasis of the collective family unit, the prestige and entitlement that their mighty bloodlines bestows, the perspective of power as a birthright. That kind of loyalty to one another also being the kind of attitude that one can expect to have them ultimately take your side when push comes to shove, even if they knew nothing of the plans beforehand.<br /> <br /> I see these things, because to me the fact that there are <i>so many</i> outcastes has for a very long time felt like an indicator that good breeding is not about Dragon Blooded <u>numbers</u>, but about <u>concentration</u>. If all you want is lots of them, there's enough of that blood spread through an ultimately pretty large population to get about as many as you need. If you want lots of them <i>all in one place</i>, then you keep them close and you make sure that each conception has the highest chances possible of producing a child that will Exalt. You couldn't have the Scarlet Realm without the kind of clan maintenance of the Dynasty because that Realm is propped up by the certainty that it will have a very large number of Exalted under your umbrella (who can then be brought up to value the kinds of family obligations that you ensure only the Realm can provide). If you didn't have the Dynasty, you could still have quite enough Exalted to safeguard the world from gods and faeries, if that was a thing you cared about more than the imperialism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T23:22:35-07:00","id":1400017,"title":"","content":"Firstly, Isator Levi, I *adore* that idea and shall apply it to my games from this point forth.<br /> Secondly, I've always personally thought that part of why the Usurpation worked like it did was the lunars, not the solar 'traitors.' Lunars fed up with their solar mates being fucking psychopaths half the time. I imagine a significant portion of them were as fed up as the other exalts, but unable to solve the problem completely. Kill one solar, now you probably got a bunch mad at you and there's still the same number of potential crazy fuckers in the world anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23941-aquatica","name":"Aquatica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23941_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T07:00:07-07:00","id":1400082,"title":"","content":"Really, even the contrast based on concentration has caveats. The Realm is evidently quite capable of concentrating all of the widely distributed thin-blooded Exalts that appear within their not inconsiderable bounds, a level of organisation and transportation that I expect is quite beyond most of the Threshold and would have been massively outdone by resources available in the First Age.<br /> <br /> I expect doing that specifically in terms of gathering them all up while young and herding them into a system of uniform indoctrination is something that only works when you've got the means and the motive to subordinate them beneath your aristocratic clan groups. I would expect that in the First Age, the standard model for the Terrestrial Exalted bore less resemblance to Great Houses than it did to the diverse range of groups one finds clustering together across the Threshold. Newly Exalted kids are less susceptible because they've got a range of competing schools to gravitate towards, who manage to keep one another in check (helped by soliciting the interests of Celestial Exalted). More personal liberty, a more cosmopolitan system. I wouldn't even think distance was much of an issue; even if one doesn't have access to a scholarship program that can pay their way from the borders of Creation to the slopes of Meru (or even the opposite border of Creation; a lot of news comes over the wire about the exciting opportunities in the desert frontiers, and you've turned out to be a Fire Aspect), I can picture a scene in which just about any bank one can access will be eager to offer loans with generous terms for the sake of establishing relations with an up-and-coming Exalt.<br /> <br /> Suddenly I'm considering the irony of the term &quot;shahan-ya&quot; having once been a more widely applied title of prestige for Dragon Blooded than Lunars.<br /> <br /> They're interesting thought exercises sure, and it gratifies some of my personal sensibilities (not least is an enduring attachment to the idea that the big family units of the Second Age were something of an innovation), but I think they could also serve as an interesting model for characters to learn of that can inform their visions for the world's future.<br /> <br /> I already kind of feel that it's the sort of thing a lot of Lunar Exalted think of, particularly in light of references to how many of them see trying to constantly kill Realm Exalted as at least counterproductive. The Scarlet Dynasty is a monopoly; you don't object to their basic existence, you've just got to break up their organisation and resources and more widely scatter it around the world. Most Dynasts who would hear of such a plan would imagine it as portending defeat in detail, but even a lot of the angrier Lunars would settle for just redistributing the power to ensure it couldn't be gathered into a big mass to bludgeon all opposition. Sure, that this would also result in a commensurate increase in Lunar power both at the individual and institutional level is a thing that is widely expected and wanted, but they can form a lot of effective arguments for it being a good thing for the world and even the Dragon Blooded in its own right.<br /> <br /> (You also get a few Dynasts that would hear of such plans, actually assess them accurately, and be more horrified by that then the prospect of Lunars then roving around picking them off one by one. You get a lot of ones very invested in their legacy for its own sake, the grandeur that comes from the collective culture of hundred of Dragon Blooded gathered in the shadow of a legendary founder and a very impressive House. The likes of Mnemon would find the idea of one's descendants living in a more modest manner and no longer perpetuating the values and standards and aesthetics that she cultivated to be quite revolting, never mind the idea that this would allow Lunars to rise above them.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}